{"availability":"available","full":"questdb/questdb","name":"questdb","description":"QuestDB is a high performance, open-source, time-series database","category":"Finance","language":"Java","stars":17421,"forks":1659,"created":"2014-04-28T23:29:15Z","updated":"2026-10-05T17:25:41Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://questdb.com","topics":["apache-arrow","capital-markets","database","historian","kdb","low-latency","market-data","parquet","quantitative-finance","questdb","real-time-analytics","robotics","scada","sql","stream-processing","telemetry","tick-data","time-series","time-series-database","tsdb"],"demo":"https://demo.questdb.io/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T19:23:25.675Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T19:23:25.675Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T19:23:25.675Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T19:23:25.675Z","stars":17421,"forks":1659}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["QuestDB is the open-source, low-latency time-series database on open formats. It ingests millions of events per second, computes on live data in milliseconds, and keeps years of history queryable. One SQL engine spans ingestion, stream processing, and tiered storage.","The engine is zero-GC Java with C++ and Rust on the hot paths. Data lives in memory-mapped, time-partitioned columns. Queries run across all cores with SIMD and JIT-compiled filters. There are no third-party dependencies on the data path.","Storage is tiered: a parallel write-ahead log, native columnar partitions, and Apache Parquet. In open source you convert partitions to Parquet with ALTER TABLE, or create a table in Parquet directly. QuestDB Enterprise converts cold partitions automatically and tiers them to object storage. Parquet, Apache Iceberg, and Apache Arrow keep the data open to any tool."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/questdb/questdb/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"d85c508fd47434729c07af97928d01b1cd54bf1